  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nA mid-level ridge will remain firmly in place over South Texas \nthrough the forecast period, supporting a prolonged stretch of hot \nand dry weather. While low-level moisture will keep dewpoints in the \nmid to upper 70s across much of the area, subsidence beneath the \nridge will suppress rainfall and favor mostly clear to partly cloudy \nskies. Afternoon highs will generally range from the mid 90s near \nthe coast to around 105 degrees across the Brush Country. \n\nThe primary concern remains the increasing heat. Heat index values \nin the 105-112 degree range are expected most afternoons, with \nlocalized values approaching 115 degrees possible later this week, \nespecially along the Coastal Bend and the Coastal Plains. HeatRisk \nwill remain moderate for much of the area while increasing to major, \nand locally extreme across portions of the northern Brush Country, \nby late week. Those without adequate cooling or hydration will be \nmost susceptible to heat-related illness.",
